Package: OneClickCartographics
Type: Package
Title: OneClickCartographics: Automated Publication-Grade Cartography for Biodiversity Science
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(person("Anonymous", "Author", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "anonymous@peer-review.org"))
Author: Anonymous Author [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Anonymous Author <anonymous@peer-review.org>
Description: Automated, publication-ready cartography and biodiversity distribution
    mapping from species occurrence tables or scientific names with a single
    function call. Features zero-configuration clean minimalist defaults, direct GBIF
    taxonomic queries, automated coordinate quality cleaning (filtering Null Island,
    inverted coordinates, and placeholder artifacts), and IUCN Red List Criterion B
    range metrics (Extent of Occurrence [EOO] and Area of Occupancy [AOO]) with
    intelligent habitat-boundary constraints (excluding unsuitable marine or terrestrial
    areas). Provides distinct taxonomic type specimen highlighting (Holotypes, Syntypes),
    multi-species comparative faceted plates, dual-metric equal-area grid aggregation
    (species richness and record density with white-to-red stepped scales and 1-pixel
    continuous contours), and journal dimension presets for major publishers (Zootaxa,
    Pensoft/ZooKeys, Nature, PLOS, Elsevier, Wiley). Also includes modular layer
    construction, interactive Leaflet web maps with hover tooltips, and automated
    Materials and Methods prose and BibTeX citation generation.
